    "data" : "189.231 State maintained highways -- Restriction and regulation of traffic.\n(1) The secretary of transportation may install and maintain traffic control devices upon\nstate-maintained highways in such manner as is reasonably necessary to promote the\nsafety and convenience of the traveling public.\n(2) The driver of any vehicle shall obey the instructions of any official traffic control\ndevice applicable thereto unless otherwise directed by a traffic or police officer,\nsubject to the exceptions granted the driver of an authorized emergency vehicle.\n(3) The secretary of transportation may restrict or regulate traffic upon state-maintained\nhighways in such a manner as is reasonably necessary to promote the safety of the\ntraveling public.\nEffective: April 10, 1988\nHistory: Amended 1988 Ky. Acts ch. 347, sec. 1, effective April 10, 1988. -- Amended\n1966 Ky. Acts ch. 255, sec. 178. -- Created 1952 Ky. Acts ch. 206, sec. 1.",
