    "data" : "189.430 Coasting prohibited -- Unattended vehicle.\n(1) The driver of a motor vehicle when traveling upon a down grade shall not coast\nwith the gears of the vehicle in neutral.\n(2) The driver of a commercial motor vehicle when traveling upon a down grade shall\nnot coast with the clutch disengaged.\n(3) No person operating or in charge of a motor vehicle shall permit it to stand\nunattended without first stopping the engine, locking the ignition and removing the\nkey, nor allow it to stand upon any perceptible grade without effectively setting the\nbrake and turning the front wheels to the curb or side of the highway.\nEffective: October 1, 1942\nHistory: Recodified 1942 Ky. Acts ch. 208, sec. 1, effective October 1, 1942, from Ky.\nStat. sec. 2739g-69i.",
