    "data" : "189.080 Horns and other sound devices.\nEvery motor vehicle, when in use on a highway, shall be equipped with a horn or other\ndevice capable of making an abrupt sound sufficiently loud to be heard from a distance of\nat least two hundred (200) feet under all ordinary traffic conditions. Every person\noperating an automobile or bicycle shall sound the horn or sound device whenever\nnecessary as a warning of the approach of such vehicle to pedestrians or other vehicles,\nbut shall not sound the horn or sound device unnecessarily. A bell may be used on a\nbicycle.\nEffective: July 12, 2006\nHistory: Amended 2006 Ky. Acts ch. 173, sec. 7, effective July 12, 2006. -- Amended\n1974 Ky. Acts ch. 101, sec. 4. -- Amended 1970 Ky. Acts ch. 93, sec. 9. -- Amended\n1952 Ky. Acts ch. 167, sec. 1, effective June 19, 1952. -- Recodified 1942 Ky. Acts\nch. 208, sec. 1, effective October 1, 1942, from Ky. Stat. sec. 2739g-28.",
