    "data" : "244.110 Retail premises to furnish clear view from sidewalk or entrance.\nThe entrance of any premises for which a quota retail package license or a quota\nretail drink license has been issued shall be of clear glass and permit an\nunobstructed view. The premises shall be erected and maintained to furnish a clear\nview of the premises from the sidewalk, or, if the premises are not on the street\nlevel, from the entrance. No partition, box, stall, screen, curtain, or other device shall\nobstruct the view or the general observation of persons, but partitions, subdivisions,\nor panels that are not higher than forty-eight (48) inches from the floor shall not be\nconstrued as obstructing the view or the general observation of persons.\nEffective:June 29, 2017\nHistory: Amended 2017 Ky. Acts ch. 62, sec. 94, effective June 29, 2017. --\nAmended 1998 Ky. Acts ch. 121, sec. 27, effective July 15, 1998. -- Recodified\n1942 Ky. Acts ch. 208, sec. 1, effective October 1, 1942, from Ky. Stat. sec.\n2554b-176."
