    "UOR" : "'02404'",
    "data" : "520.090 Resisting arrest.\n(1) A person is guilty of resisting arrest when he intentionally prevents or attempts to\nprevent a peace officer, recognized to be acting under color of his official authority,\nfrom effecting an arrest of the actor or another by:\n(a) Using or threatening to use physical force or violence against the peace officer\nor another; or\n(b) Using any other means creating a substantial risk of causing physical injury to\nthe peace officer or another.\n(2) Resisting arrest is a Class A misdemeanor.\nEffective: January 1, 1975\nHistory: Created 1974 Ky. Acts ch. 406, sec. 177, effective January 1, 1975."
