    "data" : "257.390 Importation of poultry over five months of age.\nChickens, turkeys, or other poultry over five (5) months of age intended for breeding\npurposes shall not be imported into the state unless they have passed a negative\nagglutination test for pullorum disease under the supervision of an authority of the Office\nof State Veterinarian within thirty (30) days preceding date of importation, or have\noriginated from flocks authoritatively participating in a pullorum control and eradication\nphase of the National Poultry Improvement Plan or other USDA-administered plan.\nEffective: June 29, 2023\nHistory: Amended 2023 Ky. Acts ch. 16, sec. 6, effective June 29, 2023. -- Amended\n2005 Ky. Acts ch. 115, sec. 2, effective June 20, 2005. -- Amended 2002 Ky. Acts\nch. 49, sec. 11, effective July 15, 2002. -- Created 1948 Ky. Acts ch. 165, sec. 3."
