    "data" : "311.676 Requirement for use of designation and display of license -- Prohibited\nactivities -- Penalties.\n(1) An acupuncture practitioner shall use the designation \"licensed acupuncturist\" or\n\"L.Ac.\" following his or her name in all advertisements, professional literature, and\nbillings used in connection with his or her practice.\n(2) The license issued by the board shall be conspicuously displayed in the licensed\nacupuncture practitioner's place of business.\n(3) A person who is not licensed under KRS 311.671 to 311.686 shall not use any\nterms, words, abbreviations, letters, or insignia that indicate or imply that he or she\nis engaged in the practice of acupuncture.\n(4) Any person who violates this section shall be guilty of a Class A misdemeanor.\nEffective: July 15, 2014\nHistory: Amended 2014 Ky. Acts ch. 24, sec. 6, effective July 15, 2014. -- Created\n2006 Ky. Acts ch. 249, sec. 6, effective July 12, 2006.",
