    "data" : "518.040 Sports bribery.\n(1) A person is guilty of sports bribery when he:\n(a) Offers, confers or agrees to confer any benefit upon a sports participant with\nintent to influence him not to give his best efforts in a sports contest; or\n(b) Offers, confers or agrees to confer any benefit upon a sports official with\nintent to influence him to perform his duties improperly.\n(2) Sports bribery is a Class D felony.\nEffective: January 1, 1975\nHistory: Created 1974 Ky. Acts ch. 406, sec. 159, effective January 1, 1975."
