    "data" : "318.200 Water heating devices -- Serial numbers.\n(1) No water heating device shall be sold or offered for sale in the Commonwealth of\nKentucky unless it contains a serial number on it. As used in this section, \"water\nheating device\" means any pressure vessel which heats, stores, and supplies potable\nwater for domestic or commercial purposes other than for space heating.\n(2) All retailers, wholesalers, and installers selling or offering for sale a water heating\ndevice shall, within thirty (30) days of the date of sale, forward a list of names and\naddresses of purchasers along with the serial numbers of the devices purchased to\nthe department or to the appropriate agency of county or city government having\njurisdiction.\nEffective: July 15, 2010\nHistory: Amended 2010 Ky. Acts ch. 24, sec. 1693, effective July 15, 2010. --\nAmended 1992 Ky. Acts ch. 5, sec. 1, effective July 14, 1992. -- Created 1984 Ky.\nActs ch. 272, sec. 1, effective July 13, 1984.",
